# yt-dlp

# YouTube requires solving a JS "n-signature" challenge; without a runtime the
# media URLs come back unsigned and every download 403s. Only deno is enabled
# by default, so point yt-dlp at node instead. Drop this line if deno is
# installed.

--js-runtimes node

# The challenge solver itself is not shipped with yt-dlp; fetch it from GitHub.

--remote-components ejs:github

# Some videos serve nothing but storyboards or DRM-protected formats to the
# default clients. When that happens, retry on the command line with:
#
#     --extractor-args "youtube:player_client=web_embedded"
#
# Left out here on purpose: it changes format selection for every video.
